import { EffectSequencingCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> EffectSequencingCopy = EffectSequencingCopy {
  summary: "Build a preview in small steps: check the title, require a template, then prepare the text. std/effect lets these steps share a known-failure path while the caller decides how to display the result.",
  taskTitle: "Prepare and display a release preview",
  purpose: "A preview needs a non-empty title and a supplied template. The example tries four inputs so you can see success, an invalid title, a missing template, and a present but empty template. The goal is to explain what happens at each step, including when a later step is skipped.",
  typescriptBefore: "The TypeScript version uses a plain Result object with either ok: true and value, or ok: false and reason. prepare checks that object, checks template === undefined, and returns another object. preview uses an ordinary branch to choose what to print. There are no promises or thrown exceptions here.",
  benefit: "In Seseragi, prepare can put those dependent steps in a do block. Each <- receives a successful value; a known failure stops the remaining steps in that block. attempt gives the caller a value it can inspect and display.",
  setup: "effects is the imported alias for std/effect. The ordinary fn checkedTitle returns Either<String, String>: Left carries a rejection reason and Right carries a valid title. Maybe<String> represents a template as Just some text or Nothing. These are explicit alternatives, not JavaScript truthiness checks.",
  after: [
    "effect fn prepare defines work. Its title: String and template: Maybe<String> inputs lead to a String result; fails String declares its known-failure reason. fromEither turns checkedTitle into a step, and validTitle <- names its successful value.",
    "fromMaybe supplies the missing-template reason and binds a present template to selected. succeed makes the combined text the successful result of prepare. The final line of do is the work whose result the block returns.",
    "preview calls attempt around prepare and names the resulting Either value result. The ordinary function describe uses match to select Right value or Left reason; println displays its text.",
    "preview returns Unit, meaning no useful return value, and declares with Console fails ConsoleError because printing needs console access and can fail. main runs the four previews. _ <- waits for a step while discarding its value.",
  ],
  details: [
    "The empty title fails before the template is checked, so the call with an empty title and Nothing reports title is required. A valid title with Nothing reports template is missing instead.",
    "Just \"\" is a supplied template, so the final call succeeds with an empty prefix. To reject blank templates too, add that validation explicitly; fromMaybe only checks whether a value is present.",
    "effects.succeed 42 is work that produces an integer, not an Int itself. Use <- inside do when you need its value. Likewise, fromEither needs a Left/Right result, not plain text.",
    "attempt handles the declared failure of the work it wraps. It does not turn runtime programming defects or cancellation into Left, and the later println is outside this attempt.",
  ],
}
